---
description: Model the environment accurately and keep unsafe operations at the boundary
globs:
  - "**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,mjs,cjs,d.ts}"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Environment and boundaries

- Model globals, environment variables, and build-time constants accurately using declaration files when needed.
- If code depends on `window`, `globalThis`, injected config, or custom environment variables, define them explicitly.
- Keep untyped or external input at the boundary and validate or narrow it before use.
- Localize unsafe casts to the smallest possible scope and document why they are safe.
- Prefer `async`/`await` over callbacks for asynchronous flows.
- Do not hide runtime uncertainty behind overly broad types.
